      "imageReview": "PASS recommendation with explicit identity review. All four exact images opened individually. Selected close frame has sharp eyes, muzzle, pale head band and a clear young face emerging beside maternal fur. Wider 188449563 establishes the red-brown adult and much smaller carried animal; that adult is NOT Pippa or Rudi. The gray-brown, striped juvenile is the proposed earlier Pippa. Opened existing gray adult Pippa /tmp/freed-strange07-review.Z1IsPu/1.jpg for comparison. Young body is partly occluded; no claimed proven ontogenetic color change or same real individual across photographs. Lead should judge juvenile visual compatibility independently. Exact large delivery 1024 x 683 is used; original upload metadata 2048 x 1366 was not downloaded. No crop, retouching or invented flight pixels.",
      "proseAssessment": "PASS recommendation. She hides from the very view she wanted, then asks for another journey to recover the missed experience. The desire to repeat grows from the lost view, not a lesson about courage. Pippa's earlier adult feet-versus-confidence short makes fear familiar; this adds childhood dependency and curiosity rather than another debate between her feet. Rudi's pleasure in repeated glides remains a separate adult event, not a second version of this child's missed view.",
