  "holds": [
    {
      "characterId": "penny-focus",
      "title": "Before the trembling stopped",
      "body": "I caught the wasp behind the head. For a while I held him without feeding. Every leg I had seemed to be waiting for a different part of him to move. Then I lowered my mouth. The first taste reached me before the trembling stopped.",
      "photoId": 4966716,
      "verdict": "HOLD material facial-color continuity. Excellent exact image of a gray/white female and wasp, current research-grade Phidippus regius with five matching IDs. Opened /tmp/freed-strange08-review.RUZPa1/21.jpg and /tmp/freed-visual-land02.Q6w8EB/strange-08-24.jpg: Penny has a conspicuous orange face. Female population color variation does not establish individual transformation. Do not bind or recolor. Source and full attempted body preserved for any future compatible exact scene.",
      "fictionBoundary": "Capture location, pause, fear and trembling are invented. Prey is visibly held; no prey-suffering joke or species-specific wasp ID.",
      "biologySource": "https://ask.ifas.ufl.edu/publication/IN309 opened in this batch; supports predation, female forms and natural history, not individual color change."
    },
    {
      "characterId": "mireille-tap",
      "title": "Someone had been here",
      "body": "The coconut was already open. I put a finger inside, found the white flesh and stopped. Whoever had made the hole could have eaten it. I tried a little from the far side, where their teeth might not have been.",
